  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The revolving door – turn round the cone and pass on",
  "description": "Groups of three. Place two cones in a line a few metres apart. A and C stand at either end, in line with the cones, and B stands between the cones. A has the ball.\n\nA passes to B, who moves towards the nearest cone and receives on the move. B turns tightly round the cone with the ball and plays a sweeping pass to C at the far end. Straight after, B moves to the other cone, gets the pass from C and does the same the other way. Keep it going without breaks for about a minute, then B swaps with one of the end players.\n\nVariant: A and C move sideways, so B has to look up and find the receiver before turning. Alternate turning with the ball on the forehand and on the backhand. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Receive the ball on the move, not standing still."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Turn tightly round the cone with the ball close to the blade."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Look up at the receiver before you turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Pass with a sweep, flat and all the way onto the stick."
    }
  ],
